                             globe), so the surface doesn\'t block              
                             the line of sight to B. Actually, this             
                             is a common misconception: on a sphere,            
                             distant objects don\'t disappear                   
                             because the surface curves \\"away\\"              
                             from you, not toward you, in terms of              
                             blocking.\\n\\nLet me clarify with a 2D            
                             circle: A ball. Stand on the inner...              
                             no, we\'re on the outside. You\'re at              
                             point A on the circumference looking at            
                             point B on the circumference. Draw the             
