                             *far* side (beyond the chord). It does             
                             not curve back toward you; it curves               
                             away. So you can see B. The curvature              
                             of the Earth does NOT hide distant                 
                             objects at the same                                
                             elevation.\\n\\nWhat hides distant                 
                             objects is if the object is *below* the            
                             tangent line, or if you\'re at a height            
                             and the surface curves down *away* from            
                             you below your horizon. If you\'re at              
