                             the sky where the atmosphere thins.                
                             That band is essentially flat to the               
                             eye because the atmosphere is mostly               
                             uniform.\\n\\nSo the main answer:                  
                             You\'re looking at the sky, not the                
                             ground. To see Earth\'s curvature, you             
                             need to be above the atmosphere or look            
                             at the far side of the atmosphere where            
                             it is curved. But even in space, from a            
                             window, the curvature is                           
                             small.\\n\\nLet\'s refine the                      
